// Must not compile: "undeclared identifier: io.puts is declared in io.wz; add: include
// "io.wz";" -- forgetting the include is the first mistake a newcomer makes, and the bare
// message says nothing about where io.puts lives while the compiler is carrying the
// library that declares it.
//
// tests/compiler/missing_include_quiet.sh is the other half: a name that is in no library
// must NOT get a hint, or the hint becomes noise on every typo.
begin
  io.puts(STDOUT, "hi\n");
end.
